  "Question": "If \\(x,\\) \\(y,\\) and \\(z\\) are positive with \\(xy=24,\\) \\(xz=48,\\) and \\(yz=72,\\) then \\(x+y+z\\) is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(18\\)",
    "B": "\\(19\\)",
    "C": "\\(20\\)",
    "D": "\\(22\\)",
    "E": "\\(24\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Multiplying the two products containing \\(x\\) produces \\(x^2yz\\). Dividing by the known product \\(yz\\) then removes both \\(y\\) and \\(z\\). Since \\(yz=72\\ne0\\), this division is valid:\n\\[\nx^2=\\frac{(xy)(xz)}{yz}\n=\\frac{24\\cdot48}{72}=16.\n\\]\nBecause \\(x\\) is positive, \\(x=4\\). The other two products now give\n\\[\ny=\\frac{24}{4}=6,\n\\qquad z=\\frac{48}{4}=12.\n\\]\nThese values also give \\(yz=6\\cdot12=72\\). Thus\n\\[\nx+y+z=4+6+12=22,\n\\]\nwhich is choice D.",
